# MAD vLLM patch for docker/vllm_disagg_inference.glmv5.3_quark_mxfp4_attnfp8.ubuntu.amd.Dockerfile
# What: MoRIIO hybrid (KDA) READ moves only the full-attention pages the decode side
#   does not already hold in its prefix cache. Active for hybrid models
#   (GLM-5.3-Flash); a no-op for the full GLM-5.3 model, which takes the non-hybrid
#   branch (see 0007).
# Upstream: vllm-project/vllm#62190 (open), at cdb4bbf184, unchanged.
#   https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62190
# Remove when: #62190 is merged and VLLM_REF contains it. 0007 applies on top of
#   this patch, so rebase 0007 at the same time.
# Note: the commit-message preamble below was reworded for publication; the diff
#   hunks are byte-identical to the tested patch (tested file sha256 4690a21b...).
# ---- end of MAD header; the patch follows (diff hunks as tested) ----
From cdb4bbf184e49cbc619fe5efb52772f315f4e89e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: whx-sjtu <xiaowang990929@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:05:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Bugfix][KV Connector][ROCm] MoRIIO hybrid READ: skip locally
 cached prefix pages

Hybrid (KDA/Mamba) READ paired the complete decoder attention table with
the prefill table by length and tail alignment, so a decoder prefix-cache
hit still re-read every cached page. For each full-attention group, select
the pages covering the final external token range [N-1-E, N-1) from both
complete tables instead, and raise if the tables do not cover it.
Window-clipped and state attention groups keep tail alignment.

Local patch, not yet merged upstream.
Upstream: https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62190 (open, draft)
Head: cdb4bbf184e49cbc619fe5efb52772f315f4e89e
  (whx-sjtu:whx/moriio-hybrid-read-skip-cached-prefix), taken unchanged.
PR base 5689c2790c is an ancestor of cd1effa2e7; its dependency vllm#60867
(merge 1353e1926f) is already in cd1effa2e7 and 8673602b8b. Applies with
no offsets on 8673602b8b + 0001 + 0002.
Exported: 2026-11-04.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: whx-sjtu <xiaowang990929@gmail.com>
